# The Dockerfile installs PHP extensions and nothing else — it has NO COPY or ADD,
# because all application code arrives at runtime via the bind mount declared in
# docker-compose.yml ("./:/var/www/html/TCGEngine"). So the build needs zero context.
#
# BuildKit (Docker 23+ default) already figures this out and skips transferring the
# context entirely. This file matters only for the legacy builder (DOCKER_BUILDKIT=0,
# still pinned in some CI and corporate Docker installs), which otherwise tars and
# ships the whole ~2 GB / 33k-file working tree once per web-server service — five
# times for a full `docker compose up`.
#
# ⚠ If you ever add a COPY/ADD to the Dockerfile, this WILL silently break it.
#   Un-ignore exactly what you need, e.g.:
#       !composer.json
#       !composer.lock
**
